# Netlify _redirects — converted from ops/legacy-apache/.htaccess (IONOS Apache, live until 2026-10-07)
#
# Order = Apache's effective order: in .htaccess context mod_rewrite (RewriteRule) runs BEFORE
# mod_alias (Redirect/RedirectMatch), so all RewriteRule-derived lines come first, then the
# RedirectMatch-derived lines. Netlify: first match wins; rules without "!" only apply when no
# file exists (pages are never shadowed); trailing slashes are ignored when matching.
# Verified by tests/dist/redirects.test.ts (sample table per Apache rule, DE URL contract, targets exist).
#
# NOT 1:1 EXPRESSIBLE ON NETLIFY (no regex) — what was done instead:
#  - RewriteRule ^(.+)$ /$1/ (trailing slash, l.25-29), HTTPS (l.10-11), non-www (l.14-15):
#      dropped. Netlify pretty URLs add the slash; HTTPS is automatic; www -> apex is the first rule below.
#  - RewriteRule ^index\.html/?$ / (l.397): dropped (dist/index.html exists; a forced self-rule risks a loop).
#  - Query rules ^s=(.*)$, ^p=[0-9]+$, ^page_id=[0-9]+$ on / and ^replytocom= / ^share= on any path:
#      Netlify only checks that the parameter is PRESENT (not its position or that it is numeric).
#  - RewriteRule ^(.+)/attachment/[^/]+/?$ (410): expanded to 1–3 leading segments (deeper -> 404).
#  - RewriteRule ^.*-attachment/.*$ [G] (410): substring match inside a segment impossible -> 404.
#  - RewriteRule ^5-gruende-warum-zauberei-zum-karneval-gehoert (prefix, emoji-suffixed old slug):
#      only the exact slug (+ sub-paths); emoji variants fall through to the root catch-all -> /blog/.
#  - ...kinderzauberer-in-(.*) / clown-in-(.*) / clown-in-(.+) / kinderzauberer-in-([^/]+):
#      enumerated for the 23 city pages that exist in dist/; other slugs fall to the next rule of
#      the group (Apache would have sent them to a non-existing city URL = 404).
#  - RewriteRule ^clown/([a-z0-9-]{20,})/?$ /blog/ (l.409) vs ^clown/[a-z][a-z0-9-]+/?$ 410 (l.435):
#      length cannot be checked -> every unknown single-segment /clown/<x>/ gets 410 (known old blog
#      slugs under /clown/ are mapped individually to their article above, l.407).
#  - RewriteRule ^([a-z0-9-]{20,})/?$ /blog/ with !-f !-d and excluded prefixes (l.414-417):
#      becomes "/:slug /blog/ 301" (non-forced = !-f/!-d). Length >= 20, the character class and the
#      prefix exclusion (blog|kindergeburtstag|...) cannot be checked, so ANY unknown single-segment
#      path now goes to /blog/ instead of 404. Single-segment RedirectMatch sources with another
#      target (wp-*.php, /clown, /author, /sample-page, sitemaps …) are placed before it.
#  - RedirectMatch prefix patterns ^/wp-admin(.*)$, ^/category/clown(.*)$ … : expanded to the exact
#      path + "/*"; same-segment prefixes (e.g. /category/clowns-x, /wp-adminx) fall to the next rule.
#  - RedirectMatch ^/(.*)/feed|comments|page/[0-9]+ : expanded to 1–3 leading segments; page number not checked.
#  - Dead Apache rules (shadowed by an earlier rule, never fired) are omitted: l.302 (same result via
#      l.162), l.306-310 (caught by ^content/(.+)$ -> /blog/), l.348-354 (caught by ^clown-zauberer/(.+)$),
#      RedirectMatch l.105 karneval/l.75 zaubershow overlap kept once.
#  - <Files reviews-cache.json|config.php> deny, MIME, gzip, expires, ETag: not needed / handled by Netlify;
#      Cache-Control + security headers -> netlify.toml.
#
# Pages that EXIST in dist/ but Apache redirected unconditionally -> forced with "!" (live parity):
#   /clown/clown-zauberer/ (l.357) and /zauberer/zaubershow/karneval/ (l.105, canonical already /clown/karneval/).

# ── Host: www -> apex (Apache l.14-15) ─────────────────────────
https://www.liar-entertainer.com/*                                     https://liar-entertainer.com/:splat                301!
http://www.liar-entertainer.com/*                                      https://liar-entertainer.com/:splat                301!
